<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine peso ends down,though C.Bank sells dlrs.</title>
<headline>Philippine peso ends down,though C.Bank sells dlrs.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>--------------------------- April 23-------------------------</p>
<p>*Central Bank unloads dollars at 26.37</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The Philippine peso slipped to 26.37 on Wednesday from 26.368 on dollar demand, though the Central Bank sold $44 million at the close, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Most probably it (the sale) was for commercial requirements and the bank had no choice but to buy them from the Central Bank,&quot; a foreign bank dealer said.</p>
<p>The day's average also showed a weaker peso at 26.367 from 26.362, with volume falling to $153.5 million from $166.5 million.</p>
</text>
